  "semantic_law": {
    "endpoint_constructors": "SEG(a,b) is an unoriented segment length, ANG(a,b,c) is the smaller geometric angle at b, TRI(a,b,c) is an ordered triangle. Surface endpoint order remains written even when denotations coincide. EQ is typed and cannot compare lengths to angles.",
    "sas": "APPLY_SAS(proof_id,TRI(a,b,c),TRI(d,e,f)) accepts only established equalities ab=de,ac=df and included angles bac=edf, under the ordered correspondence a->d,b->e,c->f. It returns one congruence proof whose PROJECT_SIDE/TRIANGLE/ANGLE operations must follow that SAME endpoint correspondence; they cannot return preassigned equalities.",
    "subtraction": "SUBTRACT_EQUALS(EQ(x,y),EQ(u,v),EQ(r,s)) accepts only already established same-dimension equalities plus decompositionx=u+r,y=v+s and derivesr=s. It is one polymorphic numerical law, invoked for segment lengths and angle magnitudes. Endpoint arrangement must justify each decomposition.",
    "geometry": "EXTEND and CHOOSE_ON record ordered collinear points. CUT_EQUAL requiresAE>AF and choosesG onAE withAG=AF. SAME-RAY equivalence comes only from those declared collinearities; it justifies the included common angle and the later BFC/CGB recall. No nearest-point replacement or guessed equality is allowed.",
    "claims": "STATE/GOAL describe intended propositions; GIVEN is the only axiom source besides declared constructions and standard Euclidean equality/SAS rules. SINCE,RECALL andRESTATE must retrieve facts already justified. CONCLUDE requires proof of both goals; it may not simply emit the theorem AST.",
    "source_model_assumptions": [
      "AE must be long enough for the explicitly required cut; source order supplies the construction precondition, not measured values.",
      "The final general statement is universal closure of the same nondegenerate triangle variables; empirical random-coordinate checks do not prove universal correctness.",
      "Generic subtraction is a mathematical abstraction of CommonNotion3, not a known Voynich morpheme."
    ]
